[[File:SpeakersStaff-SWBC66.png|thumb|right|75px|The Speaker's staff]]
The '''Speaker's staff''' was a long [[wood]]en [[staff]] wielded by the [[Vice Chair]] of the [[Galactic Republic]] [[Galactic Senate|Senate]]. It had crisscrossing carved lines running down its length, and was capped by a dull [[gold]]en statuette<ref name="Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> of [[Sistros Nevet]],<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref><ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref> one of the [[Four Sages of Dwartii]].<ref name="Complete Locations">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref>

During the [[proclamation of the New Order]]&mdash;when [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] announced the transformation of the Republic into the [[Galactic Empire|First Galactic Empire]]&mdash;the staff was held by the current Vice Chair, a [[Chagrian]] named [[Mas Amedda]].<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref>

After he became [[Grand Vizier]] of the Galactic Empire, Amedda continued to wield a similar [[scepter]].<ref name="HoloNet News">{{HoloNetNewsTumblr|post/98908548684/holonet-news-exclusive-mas-amedda-receives|text=Exclusive: Mas Amedda receives Governor Arihnda Pryce for Lothal report|int=HoloNet News Exclusive: Mas Amedda receives Governor Arihnda Pryce for Lothal report}}</ref> When the [[Galactic Emperor]] held a briefing, Amedda would bang his staff on the floor as a sign that the meeting should commence.<ref name="Tarkin" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Speaker's staff first appeared in the [[2005]] [[prequel trilogy]] film [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']],<ref name="Episode III" /> and was identified [[canon]]ically in the [[2016]] reference book ''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]'', written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]].<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" />

